WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.409
A private security operations dashboard is a locally controlled workspace for reviewing security alerts,

00:00:05.409 --> 00:00:08.064
events, assets, video, logs, and system health.

00:00:08.064 --> 00:00:12.615
It brings important signals together so an owner or analyst can understand

00:00:12.615 --> 00:00:16.787
what is happening without sending every record to a public service.

00:00:16.787 --> 00:00:21.717
The dashboard is an operational view, not a complete security product by itself.

00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:25.889
A SIEM collects, searches, correlates, and retains security data at scale.

00:00:25.889 --> 00:00:28.164
An NVR records and retrieves video.

00:00:28.164 --> 00:00:30.819
A ticket queue assigns and tracks work.

00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:33.853
The dashboard can surface information from all three,

00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:37.645
but it should not pretend to replace their deeper functions.

00:00:37.645 --> 00:00:39.921
Useful dashboards connect evidence to decisions.

00:00:39.921 --> 00:00:44.851
An alert should lead to relevant context, affected assets, related activity, review status,

00:00:44.851 --> 00:00:46.747
and a clear next action.

00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:49.781
Operational indicators should reveal whether cameras, collectors, storage,

00:00:49.781 --> 00:00:52.815
and alert channels are healthy enough to trust.

00:00:52.815 --> 00:00:56.229
Private-first design improves control over sensitive logs, images, credentials,

00:00:56.229 --> 00:00:57.366
and facility information.

00:00:57.366 --> 00:00:59.642
Local processing can reduce unnecessary disclosure,

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.917
preserve function during an internet outage,

00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:06.089
and let the organization define its own retention and access rules.

00:01:06.089 --> 00:01:08.364
Private does not automatically mean secure.

00:01:08.364 --> 00:01:12.157
The dashboard still needs authentication, patching, segmentation, backups, audit logs,

00:01:12.157 --> 00:01:13.295
and disciplined administration.

00:01:13.295 --> 00:01:17.466
Local systems can fail or be misconfigured just like hosted systems.

00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:20.121
The practical goal is controlled situational awareness.

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:24.293
The dashboard should help authorized people find significant events, review evidence,

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:25.051
document judgment,

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:30.740
and act responsibly while collecting no more sensitive data than the legitimate security purpose requires.
